// scripts/lib/paths-templates/broomva_paths.rs.tmpl. Do not edit: change those
// and run `python3 scripts/gen_paths.py`.
//! Where Broomva state lives: the path registry, embedded (BRO-3216, BRO-3265).
//!
//! The Rust port of `scripts/broomva_paths.py`: the same tables, the same three
//! scopes, the same migration rule on disk and in a git tree, the same containment
//! checks and the same error kinds. Read that module's docstring for the rules; this
//! one states only where the port differs. `tests/test_broomva_paths.py` replays
//! every reader call its suite makes through this module and compares the answers.
//!
//! | Python                     | Rust                    |
//! |----------------------------|-------------------------|
//! | `UnknownName`              | `Error::UnknownName`    |
//! | `ValueError`               | `Error::Invalid`        |
//! | `TreeReadError`            | `Error::TreeRead`       |
//! | `LayoutError`              | `Error::Layout`         |
//! | any other `OSError`        | `Error::Io`             |
//! | `None` (absent)            | `Ok(None)`              |
//!
//! Where it differs: Unix only (the Python reader imports `pwd`); std only and no
//! `unsafe` (Maestro forbids it), so with HOME empty the home is
//! `std::env::home_dir()` (the password database) and the account-name rule the
//! shell reader needs for its `eval` is not applied; "searchable" is an lstat of
//! `<folder>/.` where Python calls `access(X_OK)`; git runs in its own process
//! group, which a timeout kills (Python closes its pipe ends and leaves what git
//! started running); and every path and environment
//! value must be UTF-8 (anything else is `Error::Invalid`, where Python would carry
//! it as surrogates). Paths come back spelled as pathlib spells them, so `display()`
//! prints what `str(path)` prints in Python.

